evidence/native_run/actions/actions.json:316:    "action_prompt": "You are an agent who can operate an Android phone on behalf of a user. Based on user's goal/request, you may\n- Answer back if the request/goal is a question (or a chat message), like user asks \"What is my schedule for today?\".\n- Complete some tasks described in the requests/goals by performing actions (step by step) on the phone.\n\nWhen given a user request, you will try to complete it step by step. At each step, a list of descriptions for most UI elements on the current screen will be given to you (each element can be specified by an index), together with a history of what you have done in previous steps. Based on these pieces of information and the goal, you must choose to perform one of the action in the following list (action description followed by the JSON format) by outputing the action in the correct JSON format.\n- If you think the task has been completed, finish the task by using the status action with complete as goal_status: `{\"action_type\": \"status\", \"goal_status\": \"complete\"}`\n- If you think the task is not feasible (including cases like you don't have enough information or can not perform some necessary actions), finish by using the `status` action with infeasible as goal_status: `{\"action_type\": \"status\", \"goal_status\": \"infeasible\"}`\n- Answer user's question: `{\"action_type\": \"answer\", \"text\": \"<answer_text>\"}`\n- Click/tap on a UI element (specified by its index) on the screen: `{\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": <target_index>}`.\n- Long press on a UI element (specified by its index) on the screen: `{\"action_type\": \"long_press\", \"index\": <target_index>}`.\n- Type text into an editable text field (specified by its index), this action contains clicking the text field, typing in the text and pressing the enter, so no need to click on the target field to start: `{\"action_type\": \"input_text\", \"text\": <text_input>, \"index\": <target_index>}`\n- Press the Enter key: `{\"action_type\": \"keyboard_enter\"}`\n- Navigate to the home screen: `{\"action_type\": \"navigate_home\"}`\n- Navigate back: `{\"action_type\": \"navigate_back\"}`\n- Scroll the screen or a scrollable UI element in one of the four directions, use the same numeric index as above if you want to scroll a specific UI element, leave it empty when scroll the whole screen: `{\"action_type\": \"scroll\", \"direction\": <up, down, left, right>, \"index\": <optional_target_index>}`\n- Open an app (nothing will happen if the app is not installed): `{\"action_type\": \"open_app\", \"app_name\": <name>}`\n- Wait for the screen to update: `{\"action_type\": \"wait\"}`\n\nThe current user goal/request is: In Simple Calendar Pro, create a calendar event on 2023-10-16 at 13h with the title 'Appointment for Budget Planning' and the description 'We will prepare for team roles.'. The event should last for 15 mins.\n\nHere is a history of what you have done so far:\nStep 1: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"open_app\", \"app_name\": \"Simple Calendar Pro\"}. Opened Simple Calendar Pro app; now on the day view showing October 15 (Sun). Next, I should tap the \"New Event\" FAB (index 6) to create a new event.\nStep 2: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 6}. Tapped the New Event FAB (index 6); it expanded the FAB menu showing \"Task\" and \"Event\" options instead of directly opening a new event form. Next, I should click the \"Event\" option to create a new calendar event.\nStep 3: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 9}. Clicked \"Event\" FAB on the calendar day view to open the New Event creation form; the form is now displayed with empty Title/Description fields and default date October 15 (Sun) with start/end time 16:00 \u2014 I still need to change date to 2023-10-16, time to 13:00, end time to 13:15, and fill in title and description.\nStep 4: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"input_text\", \"text\": \"Appointment for Budget Planning\", \"index\": 4}. Typed \"Appointment for Budget Planning\" into the Title field (index 4) on the New Event screen; it worked as expected. Next, I need to fill in the Description, change the start date to 2023-10-16, set start time to 13:00, and end time to 13:15, then save.\nStep 5: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"input_text\", \"text\": \"We will prepare for team roles.\", \"index\": 7}. Entered \"We will prepare for team roles.\" into the Description field (index 7); it worked as the field now shows the text. Next, I need to set the start date to 2023-10-16, start time to 13:00, and end time to 13:15.\nStep 6: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 8}. Clicked the start date field (showing \"October 15 (Sun)\") to open the date picker; the calendar dialog appeared with Oct 15 selected \u2014 next I should tap on \"16\" to change the start date to October 16, 2023.\n\nHere is a list of descriptions for some UI elements on the current screen:\nUI element 0: UIElement(text='2023', content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.TextView', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=162, x_max=300, y_min=614, y_max=705), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=True, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=True, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro', resource_name='android:id/date_picker_header_year', tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\nUI element 1: UIElement(text='Sun, Oct 15', content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.TextView', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=183, x_max=640, y_min=684, y_max=789), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=True, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=True, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name=