}`\n- Press the Enter key: `{\"action_type\": \"keyboard_enter\"}`\n- Navigate to the home screen: `{\"action_type\": \"navigate_home\"}`\n- Navigate back: `{\"action_type\": \"navigate_back\"}`\n- Scroll the screen or a scrollable UI element in one of the four directions, use the same numeric index as above if you want to scroll a specific UI element, leave it empty when scroll the whole screen: `{\"action_type\": \"scroll\", \"direction\": <up, down, left, right>, \"index\": <optional_target_index>}`\n- Open an app (nothing will happen if the app is not installed): `{\"action_type\": \"open_app\", \"app_name\": <name>}`\n- Wait for the screen to update: `{\"action_type\": \"wait\"}`\n\nThe current user goal/request is: In Simple Calendar Pro, create a calendar event on 2023-10-16 at 13h with the title 'Appointment for Budget Planning' and the description 'We will prepare for team roles.'. The event should last for 15 mins.\n\nHere is a history of what you have done so far:\nStep 1: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"open_app\", \"app_name\": \"Simple Calendar Pro\"}. Opened Simple Calendar Pro app; now on the day view showing October 15 (Sun). Next, I should tap the \"New Event\" FAB (index 6) to create a new event.\nStep 2: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 6}. Tapped the New Event FAB (index 6); it expanded the FAB menu showing \"Task\" and \"Event\" options instead of directly opening a new event form. Next, I should click the \"Event\" option to create a new calendar event.\nStep 3: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 9}. Clicked \"Event\" FAB on the calendar day view to open the New Event creation form; the form is now displayed with empty Title/Description fields and default date October 15 (Sun) with start/end time 16:00 \u2014 I still need to change date to 2023-10-16, time to 13:00, end time to 13:15, and fill in title and description.\nStep 4: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"input_text\", \"text\": \"Appointment for Budget Planning\", \"index\": 4}. Typed \"Appointment for Budget Planning\" into the Title field (index 4) on the New Event screen; it worked as expected. Next, I need to fill in the Description, change the start date to 2023-10-16, set start time to 13:00, and end time to 13:15, then save.\nStep 5: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"input_text\", \"text\": \"We will prepare for team roles.\", \"index\": 7}. Entered \"We will prepare for team roles.\" into the Description field (index 7); it worked as the field now shows the text. Next, I need to set the start date to 2023-10-16, start time to 13:00, and end time to 13:15.\nStep 6: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 8}. Clicked the start date field (showing \"October 15 (Sun)\") to open the date picker; the calendar dialog appeared with Oct 15 selected \u2014 next I should tap on \"16\" to change the start date to October 16, 2023.\nStep 7: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 22}. Tapped \"16\" in the date picker to select October 16, 2023; header now reads \"Mon, Oct 16\" confirming the date is selected. Next, click OK to confirm the date, then set the time to 13:00.\nStep 8: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 6}. Clicked OK to confirm the date selection of October 16, 2023; returned to the New Event form showing the date set to \"October 16 (Mon)\". Still need to set start time to 13:00 and adjust end time to 13:15 for a 15-minute duration.\nStep 9: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 8}. Clicked the start time field (showing \"16:00\") to open the time picker; the picker appeared with 16 currently selected\u2014next I need to select hour 13 and set minutes to 00 to make start time 13:00.\nStep 10: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 10}. Clicked \"13\" on the hour clock face to set the hour to 13; it worked as the hour display now shows \"13\" and the picker advanced to the minute selection view (currently 00 selected). Next, I need to keep the minutes at 00 and press OK to confirm the start time of 13:00.\nStep 11: Action selected: {\"action_type\": \"click\", \"index\": 4}. Clicked OK to confirm the start time of 13:00; returned to the New Event screen showing start/end time both 13:00 on October 16. Next, need to set end time to 13:15 for a 15-minute duration, then click Save.\n\nHere is a list of descriptions for some UI elements on the current screen:\nUI element 0: UIElement(text=None, content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.ImageButton', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=0, x_max=147, y_min=138, y_max=285), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=True, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=True, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro', resource_name=None, tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\nUI element 1: UIElement(text='New Event', content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.TextView', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=157, x_max=414, y_min=175, y_max=249), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=False, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=False, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro', resource_name=None, tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\nUI element 2: UIElement(text=None, content_description='Save', class_name='android.widget.Button', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=953, x_max=1080, y_min=148, y_max=274), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=True, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=True, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro', resou